tweets.text:
a quickstart breaks the way an agent breaks. quietly.

@akshay_hangloo wrote that behavior kills agents, because the agent "quietly degrades instead of stopping". docs do the same. a flag gets renamed, the page stays up, and a new user finds out first.

FirstRun carries the same risk inside it. an agent that tests docs can loop on a failed command, invent a flag, and still report green.

so the plan for this weekend: every FirstRun run becomes a trace in @neatlogs. detections flag the bad runs. investigate finds why the agent failed. the fix goes back into claude code over the neatlogs MCP server.

one agent watches the docs. one tool watches the agent. #neatHack

@bettersayAJ @EntireHQ @HaimantikaM @arithecfo @agent_wrapper

#neatHack, day one. all three required tools are up.

@EntireHQ: trail #1 created, 1 checkpoint, 24.9k tokens recorded
@neatlogs: first agent trace, planner into claude-sonnet-5-5, 3 steps, 12s
